  "source" : "onDeviceDraft",
  "text" : "What I did is I took 25 microliters of the activation buffer solution and put in 500 microliters of solution G to make the activate jelling solution. Then using a pipe head. I gently sucked up and pushed out the activate geling solution inside of the Eppendorf tube to gently mix the solution to make sure tomogenized. And I took 250 microliters of the activate geling solution and put 250 microliters into 2 of the 6 wall plates where 250 microliters for each of the wells. Then I put the cover slip on top. Uh, and because this was uh, overflowing, uh, I pushed the cover slipped down to make sure a complete seal was present, uh, and the excess solution squeezed out."
